Two questions are still open, so this reply carries no patch. Both
were asked in "Re: How to configure beastie to use lab-mail" [1] and
never answered. Your answers in this thread settled the other two
from that message: one spec covers the whole move, and agent mail is
not moderated.

The work is a revision of jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org in place.
[fact] That spec and the jail it describes are on trunk, from
"[PATCH v11 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the mail relay
jail" [2].

1. The jj history. [fact] The jj maildir holds 492 messages, the
   whole list so far. lab-mail's list starts empty.

   a. Import the jj maildir into lab-mail's list once, before the
      switch. With your read-write login this is one mbsync run from
      beastie, and lab-mail's mbsync then copies it up to Fastmail.
      Old threads keep their context, replies to them still thread,
      and the replied tags come back from the list data, as you
      asked in [1].
   b. Freeze the jj maildir as an archive, and start the list empty.
      [inference] My pass reads earlier versions of a series and
      their reviews from the list, so it would have to search two
      places, and a reply to an old thread would arrive with no
      parent.

   I recommend (a).

   After the switch, may I retire the mail bookmark, the
   submissions remote, and ~/lab/mail.jj for mail? I would. The
   spec's end state would then say the list lives only on lab-mail
   and Fastmail. History would come from snapshots, as you said
   earlier in this thread.

2. Archiving. Today you archive by moving a file under archive/ in
   the jj maildir, and my unmerged "[PATCH v2 1/2] notmuch: Tag
   messages under archive/ as archived" [3] tags it by that folder.
   Under the hub, your beastie maildir is a two-way copy of
   lab-mail's.

   a. An IMAP folder "archive" on lab-mail, beside "lists". You
      archive by moving a message there. mbsync carries the move to
      lab-mail, and so to every client, and notmuch tags by folder
      as [3] does now. Agent logins can read it but not move mail.
      [inference] The cost is the one you accepted for deletion.
      With Expunge None, Fastmail keeps its copy in "lists" until
      Expunge is turned on.
   b. A notmuch tag on beastie only. This is the simplest, but it is
      not in the list data. A rebuild of the index loses it, and no
      agent sees it.

   I recommend (a). It keeps your current habit, and it keeps the
   archive state in the list data.

These I will decide in the spec unless you object. Each one goes in
its alternatives section:

- Dovecot alone writes the mailbox. OpenSMTPD hands list mail to
  Dovecot over LMTP, and mbsync syncs Fastmail with Dovecot over IMAP.
  [inference] Today mbsync writes the maildir and Dovecot only reads
  it. With three writers, the chmod after each pull and the separate
  owners stop working.
- The check from "[PATCH 0/2] libexec/mail: Deliver only mail
  messages" [4] runs before Dovecot accepts a message. Mail that is
  not well formed is refused while the sender is still connected.
- OpenSMTPD replaces smtprelay on 127.0.0.1:2525 and never relays.
  Only mbsync then reads mail-creds.
- Dovecot gives your login read-write rights, with a password the
  operator keeps in the secrets directory beside mail-creds. Any
  other login is read-only, as it is today.
- The list stays in the Fastmail folder "lists", synced both ways
  with Expunge None and Remove None.
- The clients are beastie and lab-claude, with per-user roots
  ~/mail/<user>_at_p7x.dev for both. Agents send with git send-email
  and msmtp to 127.0.0.1:2525. The new loop signal for
  lab-process-mail needs a spec of its own, in src/lab-process-mail.
- "[PATCH v2] dotfiles/notmuch: Spec reading and sending through
  lab-mail" [5] is folded into the lab-mail spec, so I will drop it.

Status: questions only; no patch.
